            ],
            [
              "CRITICAL SRS CONFLICT",
              "At 110% surge load the Pass 1 outlet temperature reaches 621°C — 1°C above the SIS trip setpoint. This means: (a) the SIF will demand on every surge operation; (b) the protection layer hierarchy is broken (NOV = DCS alarm setpoint). This SRS record CANNOT be approved until the process design is corrected. The SIF cannot be considered functional in its current form."
            ],
            [
              "Required Design Action",
              "(1) Reduce Pass 1 catalyst bed height by ~5% OR increase cold bypass valve (TCV-401) maximum Cv by 20% to lower surge outlet temperature to ≤608°C. (2) Re-set: NOV = 600°C (normal) → DCS alarm TAH = 610°C → SIS trip TSHH = 625°C. (3) Update Instrument Index, Alarm List, C&E, and this SRS simultaneously under MOC."
            ],
            [
              "Initiator(s)",
              "TSHH-401A and TSHH-401B (dual TCs, Type K multipoint, 400–700°C range)"
            ],
            [
              "Voting Logic",
              "1oo2"
            ],
            [
              "SRS Consistency Status",
              "FAIL — SIF is non-functional at surge; SRS cannot be approved in current state"
            ]
